# Two-node cluster

```elixir
Mix.install([{:elixir_harness, path: "."}])
```

Same code, two BEAM nodes. No containers — shortnames plus local epmd.

```elixir
{:ok, _} = ElixirHarness.Cluster.ensure_distributed()
{:ok, peer} = ElixirHarness.Cluster.start_peer(:demo_peer)
:ok = ElixirHarness.Cluster.ensure_app(peer.node)
tasks = for i <- 1..6, do: {ElixirHarness.Tools.Math, %{"op" => "add", "a" => i, "b" => 0}}
ElixirHarness.Orchestrator.fan_out(tasks, nodes: [Node.self(), peer.node])
```

Now the drama:

```elixir
ElixirHarness.Cluster.stop_peer(peer, :kill_9)
Process.sleep(1500)
ElixirHarness.Orchestrator.fan_out(tasks, nodes: [Node.self(), peer.node])
```

Half the batch returns `{:error, {:badrpc, _}}`, the rest succeeds.
Or run the narrated version: `mix showcase cluster`.

Tests use `:peer` nodes instead of OS processes
(`ElixirHarness.PeerCluster`): same assertions in ~0.3s, no Docker.
Requires the local epmd daemon — it usually starts itself on first use,
otherwise `epmd -daemon`.
